[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mFound 2 issue(s) in 2 file(s)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36msrc/cli.ts\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(1 issue(s))\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\r\n○ \u001b[34m\u001b[1mMEDIUM\u001b[0m ✨ \u001b[2mquality\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1msrc/cli.ts\u001b[0m:\u001b[36m182-183\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mInconsistent conditional error handling pattern\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mLines 182-183 call `log.error` and `process.exit(1)` without checking the `json` flag. This deviates from the established error handling pattern where all error logging and exits should be conditional on `!json` (see lines 94-98, 104-108, 113-116, 145-148).\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[32m→ Suggestion:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mWrap both log.error and process.exit(1) inside an `if (!json)` block, or add an else clause with JSON error output for consistency.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mAgent: consistency-check\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mRule: code-consistency\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mConfidence: 92%\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1"]
[0.000, "o", "m\u001b[36msrc/cli-schema.ts\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(1 issue(s))\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\r\n◇ \u001b[36m\u001b[1mLOW\u001b[0m ⚡ \u001b[2mperformance\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1msrc/cli-schema.ts\u001b[0m:\u001b[36m62-63\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mDuplicate string split and map operations\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mThe severity validation performs split(',').map(trim) twice - once in refine validation and again in the error message generation. This duplicates string processing work.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[32m→ Suggestion:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mExtract the parsed values before the refine check: const values = val ? val.split(',').map(s => s.trim()) : []; Then reuse 'values' in both the validation and error message.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mAgent: performance-check\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mRule: code-performance\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mConfidence: 85%\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
